              f"(will clear+relaunch once written and idle)")
    elif kind == "artifact":
        print(f"handoff armed for {sid} → {res.get('artifact_path')} "
              f"(will clear+relaunch once written and idle)")
    else:
        reason = f" ({res['reason']})" if res.get("reason") else ""
        print(f"/compact sent to {sid}{reason}")


def cmd_compact_save(args) -> None:
    """T-0467: write a TASK-LESS session's forward-state into its role artifact.

    The "write everything down" half of the universal compact — call this when
    the system asks you to hand off before being relaunched fresh. The worker
    resolves your role artifact from your session md, so you don't pass an id:
    a PROJECT-LEVEL role (operator or user-conversation) resolves to the one
    shared work-state doc — written through the concurrency lock, revisioned and
    snapshotted (T-0942) — and any other task-less role to its per-assignment
